1
00:00:03,401 --> 00:00:09,607
Mia Novak wants a price for her L-shaped kitchen. The job is built; now cost it.

2
00:00:09,607 --> 00:00:14,440
Area and cost has no money in it yet: each board shows "price (not set)".

3
00:00:14,440 --> 00:00:20,533
Prices live in the Library, on each material. Open Library, then Materials.

4
00:00:20,533 --> 00:00:30,406
White melamine carcass board: $2.85 per square foot (example prices).

5
00:00:30,406 --> 00:00:39,435
MDF: $1.95 per square foot...

6
00:00:39,435 --> 00:00:48,792
...and the 1/4" HDF backs: $0.85.

7
00:00:48,792 --> 00:00:59,756
Back to the job: the nesting now prices every sheet, by its full area.

8
00:00:59,756 --> 00:01:03,076
The job line totals all six sheets: parts, kept offcuts, scrap, and the cost.

9
00:01:03,076 --> 00:01:06,626
Sheet 3, the one with the L parts: its own share of the cost.

10
00:01:06,626 --> 00:01:19,689
For the quote, the Output tab has Areas and costs CSV: per sheet and per part.

11
00:01:19,689 --> 00:01:29,799
BOM CSV is the order list: sheets, edgeband metres, Salice hinges and plates, TANDEM slides.

12
00:01:29,799 --> 00:01:33,001
Board cost comes from the app. Edgeband, hardware and labour are priced from the BOM by hand.
